<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">How to Use This Workbook</w:t>
</w:r>
<w:bookmarkEnd w:id="6"/>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Read one chapter a week. Each chapter ends with exercises: write in the lines, tick the boxes and fill in the blanks. There are no wrong answers.</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:bookmarkStart w:name="_sec2" w:id="7"/>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Introduction</w:t>
</w:r>
<w:bookmarkEnd w:id="7"/>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">I wrote this workbook for people whose homes feel busy even when nothing is happening. You do not need a free weekend. You need ten minutes and a pen.</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:bookmarkStart w:name="_sec3" w:id="8"/>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Chapter 1: Start Where You Are</w:t>
</w:r>
<w:bookmarkEnd w:id="8"/>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Before you change anything, look at what you already do.</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Notice Your Week</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Most homes have one day that goes wrong. For me it was Sunday evening, when the week ahead arrived all at once.</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Pick One Small Corner</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">A whole house is too much to think about. A shelf, a drawer or the hall table is not.</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Keep It Short</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Ten minutes is enough. Stop when the timer goes, even if you are halfway through.</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="TakeawaysHeading"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Exercise: Your Busiest Day</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
</w:pPr>
<w:r>
<w:t xml:space="preserve">Which day of the week feels most crowded at home, and why?</w:t>
</w:r>
</w:p>
<w:p>
<w:pPr>
<w:pStyle w:val="FirstParagraph"/>
<w:pBdr>
<w:bottom w:val="single" w:color="888888" w:sz="4" w:space="1"/>
</w:pBdr>
